  "body": "## Finding description\n`OraclePack.getEMAs()` has a well-defined return order:\n\n```solidity\n// contracts/types/OraclePack.sol\nfunction getEMAs(OraclePack self)\n    internal\n    pure\n    returns (int24 _spotEMA, int24 _fastEMA, int24 _slowEMA, int24 _eonsEMA, int24 _medianTick)\n{ ... }\n```\nSo the tuple returned by getEMAs() is:\n\n`spotEMA` (index 0)\n`fastEMA` (index 1)\n`slowEMA` (index 2)\n`eonsEMA` (index 3)\n`medianTick` (index 4)\nHowever, `RiskEngine.twapEMA()` unpacks this tuple in the wrong order:\n\n```solidity\n// contracts/RiskEngine.sol\nfunction twapEMA(OraclePack oraclePack) external pure returns (int24) {\n    // Extract current EMAs from oraclePack\n    (int256 eonsEMA, int256 slowEMA, int256 fastEMA, , ) = oraclePack.getEMAs();\n    return int24((6 * fastEMA + 3 * slowEMA + eonsEMA) / 10);\n}\n```\nSolidity tuple assignment is positional, therefore this code assigns:\n\n`eonsEMA <- spotEMA`\n`slowEMA <- fastEMA`\n`fastEMA <- slowEMA`\nSo the function does not compute the intended `0.6*fast + 0.3*slow + 0.1*eons`.It instead computes `(6 * slow + 3 * fast + spot) / 10`\nThis is further confirmed by `RiskEngine.isSafeMode()`, which unpacks `getEMAs()` using the correct order:\n```solidity\n(int24 spotEMA, int24 fastEMA, int24 slowEMA, , int24 medianTick) = oraclePack.getEMAs();\n```\nMeaning `twapEMA()` is internally inconsistent with the rest of the system’s own interpretation of `getEMAs()`.\n\n## Impact\nThis incorrect TWAP tick is consumed by the protocol via `PanopticPool.getTWAP()`:\n\n```solidity\n// contracts/PanopticPool.sol\nfunction getTWAP() public view returns (int24 twapTick) {\n    twapTick = riskEngine().twapEMA(s_oraclePack);\n}\n```\n`twapTick` is then used in `dispatchFrom()` (liquidations/force exercises/settlements):\n\n- Manipulation / staleness guard uses `twapTick`:\n```solidity\nif (Math.abs(currentTick - twapTick) > MAX_TWAP_DELTA_LIQUIDATION)\n    revert Errors.StaleOracle();\n```\n- Solvency is explicitly checked at `twapTick`:\n```solidity\natTicks[1] = twapTick;\nsolvent = _checkSolvencyAtTicks(..., atTicks, ...);\n```\n- Liquidation pricing and bonus use `twapTick`:\n```solidity\n(tokenData0, tokenData1, ) = riskEngine().getMargin(..., twapTick, ...);\n(bonusAmounts, collateralRemaining) = riskEngine().getLiquidationBonus(\n    tokenData0,\n    tokenData1,\n    Math.getSqrtRatioAtTick(twapTick),\n    netPaid,\n    shortPremium\n);\n```\nAs a result, the system’s liquidation/dispatch logic relies on a TWAP that is mathematically different than intended. This can cause false positives/negatives in `StaleOracle()` checks, potentially allowing operations when the intended TWAP would block them, or blocking operations when the intended TWAP would allow them.\n\nIt can also cause incorrect solvency classification at the TWAP checkpoint (since one of the four price points in the solvency grid is wrong) ans also incorrect liquidation bonus / conversion pricing inputs (since `getLiquidationBonus` is fed `sqrtRatioAtTick(twapTick)`).\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nFix the tuple unpacking order in `RiskEngine.twapEMA()` to match `OraclePack.getEMAs()`:\n```solidity\nfunction twapEMA(OraclePack oraclePack) external pure returns (int24) {\n    (int256 spotEMA, int256 fastEMA, int256 slowEMA, int256 eonsEMA, ) = oraclePack.getEMAs();\n    return int24((6 * fastEMA + 3 * slowEMA + eonsEMA) / 10);\n}\n```\n(You can omit spotEMA if unused, but the positional order must remain correct.)",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {RiskEngine} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\nimport {OraclePack, OraclePackLibrary} from \"@types/OraclePack.sol\";\n\ncontract RiskEngineTwapEMABugTest is Test {\n    function test_POC_twapEMA_UsesWrongEMAOrdering() public {\n        RiskEngine re = new RiskEngine(10_000_000, 10_000_000, address(0), address(0));\n\n        int24 spot = 1;\n        int24 fast = 10;\n        int24 slow = 100;\n        int24 eons = 1000;\n\n        uint96 packed = OraclePackLibrary.packEMAs(spot, fast, slow, eons);\n\n        OraclePack oraclePack = OraclePackLibrary.storeOraclePack(\n            0, // epoch\n            0, // orderMap\n            packed, // EMAs\n            0, // referenceTick\n            0, // currentResiduals\n            0, // latestResidual\n            0 // lockMode\n        );\n\n        int24 twapTick = re.twapEMA(oraclePack);\n\n        // What the documentation claims: 60/30/10 weighting of fast/slow/eons.\n        int24 intended = int24((int256(6) * int256(fast) + int256(3) * int256(slow) + int256(eons)) / 10);\n\n        // What the current implementation actually does due to wrong tuple-unpack ordering.\n        int24 actual = int24((int256(6) * int256(slow) + int256(3) * int256(fast) + int256(spot)) / 10);\n\n        assertEq(twapTick, actual, \"twapEMA uses wrong EMA ordering\");\n        assertTrue(twapTick != intended, \"twapEMA unexpectedly matched intended formula\");\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\n## How to run it\nRemove this line from the `foundry.toml` file:\n```\neth_rpc_url = \"\"\n```\nbecasue when its set to an empty string, it is treated as RPC is configured, but the URL is invalid.So i got this error when i tried to run the POC:\n```\nError: invalid provider URL: \"\" (relative URL without a base)\n```\n\nSo after renoving that line, then run:\n```bash\nforge test --match-path test/foundry/types/RiskEngineTwapEMABug.t.sol -vv\n```",
